{"overview":"A painter turned tramp (Chaplin), devastated by losing the woman he was courting as a wealthy man, finds himself drunk and getting drunker by the minute with some sailors at a bar until he's literally falling down. He keeps futilely trying to draw the woman's picture on the floor with a piece of chalk until he finally passes out cold (or perhaps dies, as in the poem) at the end of the film.","cast":[{"n":"Charlie Chaplin","c":"Artist","p":"/lRI9Ky1SMOehn04OqhYJ5hQfgIK.jpg","q":"Q882"},{"n":"Cecile Arnold","c":"Madeleine","p":"/b14ZbcCn7dUwu2SCevw23zIQSwO.jpg","q":"Q5056384"},{"n":"Jess Dandy","c":"Lover who stole Madeleine","p":"/qYczONweEvAkAcsBcrmefHCC6qS.jpg","q":"Q18221268"},{"n":"Vivian Edwards","c":"Model","p":"/geFGEPk4BWpVINkfY97a4q8ULG4.jpg","q":"Q19544338"},{"n":"Chester Conklin","c":"Drinker","p":"/1W7LjVN3Fj74RsCVwA0NbLAB2re.jpg","q":"Q1070698"},{"n":"Harry McCoy","c":"Drinker","p":"/pjJnpVjuW5fe7VsAw126XnOz9Nj.jpg","q":"Q3127869"},{"n":"Hank Mann","c":"Drinker","p":"/5EGNEc8hjNmyNA6bh39czJ0BcGS.jpg","q":"Q3126801"},{"n":"Wallace MacDonald","c":"Drinker","p":"/lP3Lxz5EiWYhziMJedbkuzeaQeE.jpg","q":"Q936637"},{"n":"Fritz Schade","c":"Drinker","p":"/eh3TB68Qo30M9TFPmWONqmB3dtl.jpg","q":"Q1121639"},{"n":"Edward Nolan","c":"Bartender (as Eddie Nolan)","p":null,"q":null}],"country":["United States"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Face_on_the_Bar_Room_Floor_(1914_film)","qid":"Q2446414","rel":{"US":{"d":"1914-08-10","c":"NR"}},"backdrops":["/7tzQhQB9XWdotvNgMN8Vws0rmk9.jpg"]}